<Project Sdk="BHS.Revit.Sdk/1.6.5">

    <!--
      The assembly the probe pane's content needs and nothing else in the probe's deployment names.

      It exists for one question, and the question had no asker until 2026-09-20: does a pane's content
      find the assemblies that sit beside it? The host loads the content itself - Revit never sees its
      class name - and until that day the host loaded it in a way that left its dependencies unfindable
      on the .NET axis. The sweep was green through all of it, because BHS.Revit.Probe.Pane referenced
      only assemblies that something else had already loaded by the time the pane was shown: the check
      was vacuous by construction, and nothing said so.

      So this assembly is deliberately the only thing the pane content needs that nobody else brings in.
      That is what makes the check honest, and it is also what makes it fragile in the one direction
      that matters: NOTHING ELSE MAY REFERENCE IT. A reference from the probe, from its Entry assembly,
      from the declaration or from the pane's own feature would load it at startup, and the pane would
      find it already there - green, and about nothing. The sweep asks that too, in every mode: it is
      not loaded while no pane has been shown.

      A satellite of its own, for the second half of the same question. A .resources assembly is found
      in <culture> beside its parent by the runtime - measured outside Revit, on the default context and
      on a context of one's own - but whether the deployment carries it into Lib\ru-RU, and whether
      Revit's own context finds it there, is answered only by a sweep. The probe records the answer as a
      note until one does.
    -->

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFrameworks>net48-revit2024;net8.0-revit2025;net8.0-revit2026;net10.0-revit2027</TargetFrameworks>
        <RootNamespace>BHS.Revit.Probe.Pane.Support</RootNamespace>

        <!-- Nothing of Revit is named here, and nothing needs to be: the point of this assembly is that
             it is an ordinary dependency of the pane's content. -->
        <UseRevitApi>false</UseRevitApi>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
